WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.870
The first trailer for Avengers: Infinity War
has already provided Marvel fans a ton of

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:10.140
clues about what's to come in the newest superhero
smash, featuring the old guard and the newcomers

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.300
working together to defeat Thanos.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:16.380
But there are some aspects of the teaser that
might not be so obvious upon first review.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:21.000
Let's take a look at some of the finer details
in Infinity War's first trailer that might

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.780
hold more significance than you think.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:24.640
The hero hotline

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.860
When Tony Stark is shown visiting Doctor Strange's

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.300
Sanctum Sanctorum, there's an interesting
little Easter Egg contained in his hands:

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.100
the same cell phone that Steve Rogers gave
him at the tail end of Civil War.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.720
Even though the two didn't completely resolve
their differences, Steve apologized for withholding

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.900
the truth about Bucky's assassination of Tony's
parents in a note that also read:

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.940
"I know you were only doing what you believe
in, and that’s all any of us can do, it’s

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:49.950
all any of us should.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:54.160
So, no matter what, I promise you, if you
need us, if you need me, I'll be there."

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:58.620
Cap may be enjoying asylum in Wakanda, but
it's clear Tony's going to take him up on

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.240
that offer in Avengers: Infinity War once
the threat of Thanos becomes clear.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:03.940
New shield

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.820
In the trailer, T'Challa the Black Panther

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:07.320
instructs:

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.740
"Get this man a shield."

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:13.090
He's talking, of course, about getting Steve
Rogers back into superhero action—and the

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:16.460
line also serves as a clever callback to the
characters' comics history.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:22.580
In 1941, the Captain earned the trust of T'Challa's
father T'Chaka, who gave him a piece of Wakandan

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:26.250
vibranium —which was then used to help form
Cap's circular shield.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:31.280
Decades later, when Rogers gave up the title
of Captain America in a dispute with the U.S.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.540
government, he was gifted a new vibranium
shield by Black Panther.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.620
Now a nomad?

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.160
Steve isn't the only one sporting a new appearance
in the trailer.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.180
There's also a subtle difference in the way
Bucky is outfitted, as the star looks to be

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:45.720
missing from his new bionic arm.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:50.340
Since it was lasered off of him by Tony Stark
in the same battle that cost Cappy his shield,

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:55.200
Bucky too might've decided to shed a piece
of his pre-Civil War identity and go forward

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.000
as a non-Winter Soldier nomad.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.840
Has he rid his mind of all that pesky HYDRA
programming at long last?

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.000
Sebastian Stan has cast doubt on how well
that would work out for him, telling The Daily

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:07.890
Beast:
"I think Bucky represents some of those people

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.440
that come back and just don’t know how to
restart their lives."

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.260
A new Vision

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.140
In the first new glimpse we get of Vision

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:17.660
in Infinity War, he looks a lot more human
than he used to.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:22.520
His appearance is almost ordinary, save for
the bright yellow stone embedded in his forehead.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:26.780
In the comics, a defining feature of J.A.R.V.I.S.'s
post-download existence is that he wants to

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:28.159
be as human as possible.

00:02:28.159 --> 00:02:32.110
So, the fact that he's now been able to shed
all the red -- at least for a while -- means

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:36.510
that either someone's fantasizing about what
might've been or he's figured out some way

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.780
to shapeshift into his desired reality.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:43.620
In either case, he's clearly developed a romantic
relationship with the Scarlet Witch, which

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.720
is also a nod to a central component of his
comics origins.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:51.010
The two have had quite a storied relationship
throughout the years — often tumultuous,

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:56.280
but also resulting in twins named Wiccan and
Speed, who both end up on Young Avengers during

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.200
their teenage years.

00:02:57.389 --> 00:03:01.919
A certain casting call for Avengers 4 seems
to indicate that the latter part, at least,

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.180
will come to fruition.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.140
Blondes have more fun?

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.920
Natasha Romanoff is another of the exiled
Avengers who's seen sporting a new look in

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:11.380
Infinity War's first-glimpse.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:15.699
Rather than the dark auburn 'do that's been
her trademark all these years, she's shown

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:16.720
with blonde locks.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.660
She's probably still a fugitive at the start
of this movie, and the hue of her 'do may

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.620
just be a simple effort to disguise herself
from the government.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:28.400
However, some suspect it might also harken
back to the comics' second Black Widow character,

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.780
Yelena Belova, who sported similarly blonde
locks.

00:03:31.969 --> 00:03:36.640
If she is just trying on a new identity for
size, why not make it her alter ego one plucked

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:39.140
from the page as a hat-tip to her comic fans?

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:40.860
Frozen in time?

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:46.060
Although we don't know for sure if Thanos
has or will be able to steal the Time Stone

00:03:46.079 --> 00:03:50.349
from the Sanctum Sanctorum, there's at least
one shot in the trailer which hints that time

00:03:50.349 --> 00:03:52.080
is being messed with in some way.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:56.680
As Tony Stark is shown on the street, removing
his glasses in disbelief, the rest of his

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:59.400
friends seem to be left in a frozen state
behind him.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:04.159
What's more is that those mystical shields
seem to be turning very slowly, if at all.

00:04:04.159 --> 00:04:08.309
Does this mean that Thanos will get his hands
on that powerful green gem despite the heroes'

00:04:08.309 --> 00:04:09.140
best efforts?

00:04:09.309 --> 00:04:12.739
Or is Stark somehow commanding the Time Gem
in this scene?

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:13.320
Time...will tell.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:17.680
Nick Fury the storyteller
Although we don't actually see him in the

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:22.229
trailer, we do get to hear Nick Fury's voice
chime in on the group storytelling project

00:04:22.229 --> 00:04:24.280
that tells us how the Avengers came to be.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.340
"There was an idea."

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:31.820
He's joined by other characters to finish
out the narrative, but his inclusion is important

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:35.980
because the phrase is an almost exact replica
of the speech he gave in the first Avengers

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:36.480
movie.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:41.560
Samuel L. Jackson has said he will not appear
in Infinity War, Avengers 4 or Black Panther,

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:43.560
but could this be a sign that something's
changed?

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.540
If not, at least we know Fury will be there
in spirit.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:47.880
Thanks for watching!

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.500
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:53.240
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

